# Accepted container-image findings for the Trivy gate in .github/workflows/security-scan.yml.
# One ID per line, with the image, the reason and an expiry, after which the finding fails the
# build again, e.g.:
#
#   # keycloak: only reachable through the admin console, which isn't exposed. Recheck on 26.9.
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31

# api (usr/bin/pebble, from the mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet base image) and web (usr/bin/caddy,
# from caddy:2-alpine): Go standard library DoS fixes (Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2), not yet in either
# upstream image. Neither binary is ours to rebuild; Dependabot's digest bumps bring the upstream
# rebuilds. Recheck when this expires.
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-11-15
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-11-15
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-11-15

# api (usr/bin/pebble) and web (usr/bin/caddy), same upstream images as above: Go standard library
# crypto/x509 fix (Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3), not yet in either upstream image. Pebble only supervises
# the API process, and the web image's Caddy serves static files and doesn't verify client
# certificate chains. Recheck when this expires.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-19

# web (usr/bin/caddy, from caddy:2-alpine): go-jose v4.1.5 DoS when parsing JWKs with RSA keys,
# fixed in 4.1.6 but not yet in the upstream image (already on the newest caddy:2-alpine digest).
# The web image's Caddy only serves static files on :80 and does no ACME or JWT handling, so it
# never parses a JWK. Dependabot's digest bump brings the rebuild. Recheck when this expires.
CVE-2026-116587 exp:2026-11-15

# keycloak (guava 33.6.0, bundled by quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.8.1, the newest release): Guava
# DoS, fixed in 33.7.2. Swapping a jar inside Keycloak's distribution isn't supported; the fix
# arrives with the next Keycloak release. Recheck when this expires.
CVE-2026-102554 exp:2026-11-15
